   "source": [
    "-> Perceptron model\n",
    "    $ inputs -> Function -> Output\n",
    "    $ inputs with weigths -> function -> output\n",
    "    $ When the input is zero we will always get zero and to solve that we can add a bias term to the inputs.\n",
    "-> Multilayer perceptron has multiple layers in the perceptron.\n",
    "    $ each input in the layer connects to the next layers each input\n",
    "-> input layer => hidden layers  => output layer\n",
    "-> As the layers network increases it will become into a blackbox.\n",
    "-> Deep neural netwrok has 2 or more hidden layers.\n",
    "-> z = wx + b is the input variable.\n",
    "-> Activation functions make the values to a certain range.\n",
    "    $ f(z) is the activation function.\n",
    "    $ Step function is the basic function which outputs 0 or 1. Small changes are not reflected in this.\n",
    "    $ Sigmoid function is more sensitive to small changes. \n",
    "    $ Hyperbolic tanget: tanh(z) outputs to -1 to 1.\n",
    "    $ Rectified Linear Unit (ReLu) is a relatively simple function which is represented as max(0,z) which symbolizes that if it is less than zero then it is made equal to zero else z.\n",
    "        $ It is very good especially while dealing with vanishing gradient problem.\n",
    "-> Multiclass has two main types of situations:\n",
    "    $ non-exclusive classes -> this will have multiple classes/categories assigned to a single data point\n",
    "    $ Mutually exclusive classes -> only one class per data point.\n",
    "-> We could have multiple nuerons for each class meaning multiple outputs.\n",
    "    $ We can use the one hot encoding to make it mutually exclusive.\n",
    "    $ For each function will have a output that can be given input to the sigmoid function to output the values between 0 to 1 for each class. This gets the answer independent to other classes.\n",
    "    $ Softmax function calculates the probability distribution for the k different events.\n",
    "    $ We can use the softmax fuction for the mutually exclusive classes since all the probabilities sum up to 1.\n",
    "-> Cost functions\n",
    "    $ 1/2n * square of (sum(true values - output of the activation function))\n",
    "    $ Adaptive gradient decent tries to take the smaller and smaller steps as we go near the minimum.\n",
    "    $ Adam is a advaced and optimized alogrithm.\n",
    "    $ For classification we will be using cross entropy for loss.\n",
    "    $ Backpropagation \n",
    "-> "
   ]
